## Changelog

```
G.3b  Replaced. Ordinal and index replies no longer rejected;
      identification of a bank entry populates the slot directly.
      Rejection form conflated affirmative selection with silence.
      Narrowing variant (G.3b′, proposed) declined: narrowing a
      valid generic answer is refinement, not discovery, and falls
      outside Goal's question budget. Under-resolution accepted at
      this layer. Referential matching bounded to exactly-one to
      keep matching mechanical rather than plausibility-based.
G.3a  Render order fixed as alphabetical (dependency of G.3b
      positional matching).
§D.9a Cross-reference gloss corrected; no-new-noun scope unchanged
      and still system-side only.
§7    Echo-control basis narrowed; see note in clause.
§6    Out-of-scope entry qualified.
```

---

Goal folds in on apply. One item passes to maintenance rather than closing: §7's echo figure was calibrated with ordinal rejection contributing, so whatever number it carries is now optimistic. The note prevents it being read as a guarantee, but the figure itself wants re-deriving against live transcripts — measurement, not design.

Nothing else outstanding. If a grep turns up a fifth `G.3b` site or Hunk 5's anchor doesn't match, paste the line and I'll patch it.
